<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0000713> rdfs:label "Agitation"@en ;
    dcterms:description "A state of excessive motor activity that is associated with mental distress or a feeling of substantial unease or inner tension. Distinguished from restlessness by the increased level of emotional distress and negative intensity of the experience. Agitation has a significant level of physical activity that is typically threatening to the self or others."@en ;
    ns1:category ns1:PhenotypicFeature ;
