<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0001019> rdfs:label "Erythroderma"@en ;
    dcterms:description "An inflammatory exfoliative dermatosis involving nearly all of the surface of the skin. Erythroderma develops suddenly. A patchy erythema may generalize and spread to affect most of the skin. Scaling may appear in 2-6 days and be accompanied by hot, red, dry skin, malaise, and fever."@en ;
    ns1:broad_synonym "Red scaly skin caused by inflammatory skin disease"@en ;
    ns1:category ns1:PhenotypicFeature ;
