<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_6000933> rdfs:label "Koebner Phenomenon"@en ;
    dcterms:description "The appearance of new skin lesions on previously unaffected skin secondary to trauma. This phenomenon is also termed the isomorphic (from Greek, equal shape) response, given the fact that the new lesions that appear are clinically and histologically identical to the patient's underlying cutaneous disease." ;
    ns1:category ns1:PhenotypicFeature .

