<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0000967> rdfs:label "Petechiae"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Petechiae are pinpoint-sized reddish/purple spots, resembling a rash, that appear just under the skin or a mucous membrane when capillaries have ruptured and some superficial bleeding into the skin has happened. This term refers to an abnormally increased susceptibility to developing petechiae."@en ;
