<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0004942> rdfs:label "Aortic aneurysm"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Aortic dilatation refers to a dimension that is greater than the 95th percentile for the normal person age, sex and body size. In contrast, an aneurysm is defined as a localized dilation of the aorta that is more than 150 percent of predicted (ratio of observed to expected diameter 1.5 or more). Aneurysm should be distinguished from ectasia, which represents a diffuse dilation of the aorta less than 50 percent of normal aorta diameter."@en ;
    ns1:category ns1:PhenotypicFeature ;
    ns1:exact_synonym "Aortic dilatation"@en,
        "Bulge in wall of large artery that carries blood away from heart"@en,
        "Enlarged aorta"@en ;
