<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0025343> rdfs:label "Lupus anticoagulant"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Presence of lupus anticoagulant (LA) autoantibodies. LA represent a heterogeneous group of autoantibodies, IgG, IgM, or a mixture of both classes, that interfere with standard phospholipid-based coagulant tests (this is only an in vitro phenomenon, LA do not cause reduction of coagulation in vivo). The antibodies are directed against plasma proteins which also bind to phospholipid surfaces."@en ;
    ns1:category ns1:PhenotypicFeature .

