<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0018768> rdfs:label "familial cold autoinflammatory syndrome"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Familial cold urticaria (FCAS) is the mildest form of cryopyrin-associated periodic syndrome (CAPS) and is characterized by recurrent episodes of urticaria-like skin rash triggered by exposure to cold associated with low-grade fever, general malaise, eye redness and arthralgia/myalgia."@en ;
